# DCLF's CPU pipeline in native mode (docs/development/parity/dclf-cpu.md): Whiterun at midday GPU-driven, with the forward family
# drawn through the CPU forward site, then Dragonsreach CPU-driven (Auto: interiors on the CPU), each in third and first person with a
# torch. Look for "[DCLF] graph conditions: ... forward draws on the CPU" (exterior) and "... CPU pipeline" (interior), the [CPU]
# report line with site runs and draws, "[DCLF] site stats" lines, and no "[DCLF] CPU pipeline:" errors. Shots: smoke over the logs
# and fire behind it in the right order, the hearth and torch flame, first person's arms and torch.
# cs-ab: disable-mod=Skyrim Engine Telemetry
# cs-ab: disable-mod=ImprovedCameraSE
CS_ORG_NATIVE=1
CS_DISABLE_FEATURES=Upscaling
CS_DCLF_SITE_STATS=1
DXVK_DEBUG=hang
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=*nsight*
CS_DCLF_TEST_COMMANDS=300:set timescale to 0;301:set gamehour to 13;400:coc Whiterun;1300:tai;1500:dclf:shot=whiterun;1520:player.additem 1d4ec 1;1530:player.equipitem 1d4ec;1540:dclf:pov=first;1800:dclf:shot=whiterun-fp;1820:dclf:pov=third;2000:coc WhiterunDragonsreach;3000:dclf:shot=dragonsreach;3020:dclf:pov=first;3300:dclf:shot=dragonsreach-fp
CS_DCLF_TEST_EXIT=3400
